  "notes": "Bro-country-into-ballad specialist — party cuts and grief ballads from the same writer's pen. The drum grammar is the entry's two-lane statement: \"the party cuts use the bro-country layered kit (programmed clap, 16th hats, sampled kick, banjo-as-percussion) with stop-time drops, while the ballads run on cross-stick and shaker with the kit entering at the chorus,\" so the model carries both the clap layer and the cross-stick flag, with a real drop-out figure. Harmony is \"I–V–vi–IV, I–IV–V, and vi–IV–I–V on the ballads.\" Melody is \"mid-baritone, conversational, narrow verse range, chorus a fifth up on a repeated cell; the ballads use long sustained notes and no ornament,\" which is a high two-bar cell repeat with an octave-jump probability near the floor. ⚠ The entry describes \"synth sub plus electric bass on the party cuts; live bass alone on the ballads\" — the sub does not replace the bass on either lane, so no `drums.bass808` block is authored and the model keeps the genre's inherited live bass. ⚠ Confidence is medium, matching the research; the per-track readings are [LOW-CONF] and the entry notes one single reads ~69 or ~138 at the double. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are the clap offsets, the perc density and the counter ratio.",
